      <li data-correct="false" data-why="The kernel still runs on the unisolated cores (0-3 here), so the system functions normally. isolcpus carves out cores, it doesn't shut down the kernel.">The kernel can no longer schedule any work, so the rest of the system stops.</li>
      <li data-correct="false" data-why="Pinning prevents migration BETWEEN cores; it doesn't change cache size. Each core still has its own L1/L2 of the standard size.">Core 5's L1 and L2 caches double in size because no other process can use them.</li>
