      <li data-correct="true"  data-why="Right. PGO consistently gives another 5-15% on top of -O3 -flto, because the compiler now knows from a real run which branches are hot, which functions to inline, and how to lay out basic blocks. Cheap to set up; real wins.">Add Profile-Guided Optimization: build with <code>-fprofile-generate</code>, run a representative workload, rebuild with <code>-fprofile-use</code>.</li>
      <li data-correct="false" data-why="Switching compilers gives variable, usually small differences. PGO is a cheaper and more reliable next step.">Switch the compiler from g++ to clang++ for better autovectorization.</li>
      <li data-correct="false" data-why="A bigger NIC helps network latency. It does nothing for the CPU-side strategy code, which is what the team has been optimizing.">Buy a faster network card to reduce I/O latency.</li>
